entations, lineage, and features remain outside the selected population.","Compiler conformance, runtime performance and scheduling, complete history, and cross-version compatibility beyond explicitly cited language changes.","Claim revisions on explicit or evidence-based hold are outside this release selection."],"limitations":["The selected editions, constructs, and history statements cover a subset of the candidate population and available research dimensions.","The source-to-output mapping is the frozen SCES payload and exact linked registry entities. The candidate excludes upstream source text and code.","Proposed Apache-2.0 distribution terms apply to the original Software Commons records and annotations, subject to separate authorization.","C edition identity uses IEC catalog evidence. Technical C findings are limited to WG14 N3220.","The Python implicit-class observation applies to the recorded Windows AMD64 CPython 3.13.0 context. The Visual Basic claims are restricted to the cited Microsoft editions and archive examples.","The governing-source investigation of 47 scoped predecessor planning rows is still open. The census is not a closed language universe.","The vendor SQL dialect records leave the original regex facility lead mappings open. RPG IV and TSO/E REXX retain original-locator access gaps.","The SETL archive records distinguish languages, dialects and implementations. The ISETL link applies to the language referent. The Enterprise COBOL claim applies to the exact documented implementation and leaves conforming behavior outside scope.","The Java technical claims apply to specification edition 21. The census and research profiles remain incomplete.","Prolog chronology and the exact NIP relationship remain unresolved. The historical Prolog records apply to their documented original design.","The resolved SAP links apply to the inspected title, edition and language. The broad ABAP CDS labels retain an open distinction between DDL and DCL.","The classifier links apply only to their assessed programming-language referents. Other file usage, editions, compatibility, and broad alias scopes remain distinct.","Four original ALGOL archive anchors retain overlapping language or implementation scopes.","The broad Oberon classifier remains open. The distinct new Oberon-2 lead is provisional.","The mixed Oberon classifier remains unresolved. The Oberon-2 claims apply to the reported design.","The three exact base-format exclusions are discovery findings. The related selector, schema, encoding, and host-language behaviors require separate evidence.","The SETL variadic read-write parameter case remains unresolved. The PARLOG meta-call claim applies only to the documented proposal.","The three STRling crosswalks identify existing host SQL dialects. Exact installed engines, package configuration, and observed runtime behavior are outside those decisions."],"previous_report":{"path":"sces/releases/verified-language-cohort-rc8/qualification.json","sha256":"b123c427ef3ad52b0e36018327a77f086e0cb8789c9bf8c37d39080605ffc447"},"release":"verified-language-cohort-rc9","research_cutoff":"2026-11-23T10:04:03Z","schema_version":"registry-v1","scope":"Publisher-scoped language identities and selected technical or historical facets for ABAP, ABAP CDS DDL, Ada, Argus, CLU, COBOL, Clojure, Delphi Object Pascal, ECMAScript, Gallina, Go, Haskell, Icon, Informix 4GL, Kotlin, Lua, MUMPS, Modula-3, NESL, Napier88, Oberon, Pascal, PeopleCode, PostgreSQL SQL dialect, Python, REXX, RPG IV, Rust, SIMULA 67, SQL, SQLite SQL dialect, Scala, Visual Basic for .NET, Wolfram Language, XML, XPath. The candidate also covers source-scoped C, classic Visual Basic and its 6.0 edition, VBA, VBScript, and additional Python 3.13.0 and ECMAScript 2024 technical depth. The successor adds Java SE 21, SETL family and vendor SQL dialect records, the exact Gallina origin bridge, and the documented Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 implementation relationship. The successor includes scoped Prolog and PARLOG archive research, SQR for PeopleSoft, ABAP CDS DCL and additional SAP ABAP evidence. The successor adds scoped Java SE 21 execution and concurrency findings and nine independently agreed language-referent links. The successor adds scoped ALGOL 68 and ALGOL-N archival records and resolves the Ada original at language level. The successor includes the Oberon-2 report dialect, scoped GraphQL, Protocol Buffers schema and TOML profiles, and technical research in ISETL, SETL and PARLOG.","source_commit":"218456e77d6eedff90b4819c7146da4aab1b1485"}
